  "id": "GHSA-rj3x-4hxh-9859",
  "aliases": [],
  "title": "Cross-group authorization bypass in group inbox email replies",
  "summary": "### Impact\r\nAn authorization bypass in group inbox email processing could allow an external sender to be added to, read, and reply to a private group conversation belonging to a different group.\r\n\r\nThis only affects sites where the `email in` site setting is enabled and at least one group with an incoming email address has \"Allow unknown sender topic replies\" enabled. This is not the default.\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\nDisable \"Allow unknown sender topic replies\" (group page > Manage > Email) on every group that has it enabled. Replies from unknown senders to those groups will then create new topics instead.",
  "published_at": "2026-11-10T17:37:47.000Z",
